mods: _artprobe
timeout: 120s
hide: false
# Back-facing probe (2026-10-22, T3 card pr-cat-back): a cat facing AWAY plays its <anim>B frame, which places the
# back rig the editor now authors (cat-rig.ts newCatAnimation: probeBackPoseBack, facing "back" — head_back behind
# the body, the tail in front, vanilla idleB's layout and slot matrices; seven EMPTY slot sprites). probe.swf's
# _Append_CatTest donor carries probeBackF (the front rig, NO marker) and probeBackB (the back rig + the checker
# marker at the non-slot depth 15), so our marker appears only when the B frame plays.
# ArtProbeCatFacing = TomTom + alt_animations [[idle probeBack]] at the default enemy facing (the control: F, no
# marker); ArtProbeCatBack = the same with an orientation key (meant to face it away: the B label —
# Character_SetOrientation 0x10ce50) — OBSERVED 2026-10-22 not to turn a spawned cat (lock alone, [1 0] and [0 -1]); now
# start_orientation + lock_orientation [0 -1]. ArtProbeCatBackShown's probeBackShowF / probeBackShowB both place the
# back rig, so its shots show the back pose whatever the facing. No _autoplay: nobody acts, nothing turns or hits.
# editor/scripts/art-probe.ts --cat-back reads the shots (probe-outcomes.ts catBackOutcome): no marker in "front",
# our marker in the back (or shown) shots with a TomTom-sized outline (the cat's own parts) under it.
wait frames 120
seed 42
enter TacticsTest
wait frames 300
shot "baseline"
cmd spawn TomTom
expect console "Spawned TomTom" within 10
wait frames 120
shot "vanilla"
cmd spawn ArtProbeCatFacing
expect console "Spawned ArtProbeCatFacing" within 10
wait frames 90
shot "front"
cmd spawn ArtProbeCatBack
expect console "Spawned ArtProbeCatBack" within 10
wait frames 90
shot "back 1"
wait ms 200
shot "back 2"
wait ms 200
shot "back 3"
cmd spawn ArtProbeCatBackShown
expect console "Spawned ArtProbeCatBackShown" within 10
wait frames 90
shot "shown 1"
wait ms 200
shot "shown 2"
quit
